Space Explorer is a Python-based interactive game designed to demonstrate the integration of algorithmic logic, real-time graphics, and user interaction. Developed using the Pygame library, the game combines elements of pathfinding algorithms and procedural maze generation to create an engaging space navigation experience.

In the game, the player controls a space shuttle navigating through a dynamically generated asteroid field to collect energy orbs and reach a docking station. Each level is procedurally generated using the A* (A-star) pathfinding algorithm, ensuring unique and solvable challenges every time. The game includes features like automatic shuttle rotation, smooth animations, particle effects, and a live HUD displaying score, steps, time, and remaining orbs.

The project demonstrates the use of event-driven programming, mathematical modeling, and game physics within Python. It serves as an example of how theoretical computer science concepts such as heuristic-based search and algorithmic problem-solving can be applied to develop interactive and visually dynamic software.

Overall, Space Explorer showcases creativity, programming proficiency, and logical design, providing both educational and entertainment value while reinforcing core computational concepts.
